# Docker build context -- an ALLOW-LIST, not a deny-list (D-29, DLVR-06).
#
# The `*` below must stay the first line. It excludes the entire working tree;
# each `!` line under it re-includes exactly one path the wheel build reads.
# Move `*` down, or drop it, and every `!` line becomes decoration while the
# whole working tree is sent to the daemon -- including a real config.toml with
# a live paperless-ngx token, which is then recoverable from the build cache and
# from the discarded builder stage.
#
# This is one of TWO independent gates. The other is the explicit `COPY` lines
# in the builder stage of the Dockerfile, which replaced `COPY . .`. A mistake
# in either one alone cannot leak a secret into a layer; both would have to be
# wrong at once.
#
# README.md and LICENSE are NOT optional. pyproject.toml declares
# `readme = "README.md"` and the PEP 639 `license-files = ["LICENSE"]`, and
# `uv build --wheel` fails outright when either file is missing from the
# context. uv.lock is not read by the wheel build, but it costs nothing and
# keeps a future `uv sync --locked` in the builder stage possible.
#
# `!src/` re-includes the directory and everything beneath it; `!src/**` is not
# needed. Pinned by tests/test_deployment_config.py -- nothing else in CI would
# notice this list being weakened (D-30).
*
!src/
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!LICENSE
